[" Due to the complexity of the task, I'll provide you with a high-level design and code snippets for key components of the distributed caching system.

1. **Caching System Interface**

```java
public interface Cache<K, V> {
    void put(K key, V value);
    V get(K key);
    void remove(K key);
    void clear();
}
```

2. **DistributedCacheImpl**

The core implementation of the distributed caching system. It handles data retrieval, deserialization, and version management.

```java
import com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.*;
import java.io.*;
import java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;
import java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentMap;
import java.net.*;

public class DistributedCacheImpl<K, V> implements Cache<K, V> {
    private final ConcurrentMap<K, Future<Object>> cache = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
    private final Serializer serializer;
    private final String dataSourceUrl;

    public DistributedCacheImpl(Serializer serializer, String dataSourceUrl) {
        this.serializer = serializer;
        this.dataSourceUrl = dataSourceUrl;
    }

    @Override
    public void put(K key, V value) {
        // Implement put method, consider caching eviction policy based on LRU, LFU or ARC etc.
    }

    @Override
    public V get(K key) {
        Future<Object> future = cache.get(key);
        if (future != null && !future.isDone()) return (V) future.getNow();

        Callable<Object> callable = () -> {
            try {
                Object object = fetchFromDataSource(key);
                if (object == null) return null;
                VersionedObject<V> versionedObject = serializer.deserialize(object, VersionedObject.class);
                if (!versionMatches(versionedObject)) revalidateAndUpdateCache(key, versionedObject);
                return versionedObject.getValue();
            } catch (IOException | InterruptedException | ExecutionException e) {
                // Handle exceptions and update cache with default value or error indication
            }
        };
        Future<Object> future = executorService.submit(callable);
        cache.putIfAbsent(key, future);
        return (V) future.getNow();
    }

    // Implement other methods for remove, clear, version management etc.
}
```

