[" Below is a high-level design for the distributed logging system in C# that satisfies the requirements you've provided. Please note that this is not the actual implementation code; it provides an outline of the key components and their functionalities.

1. Create a load balancer service responsible for managing the distribution of incoming log entries across server nodes based on real-time CPU, memory, and network utilization metrics. Implement dynamic load balancing by adjusting the number of concurrent log entries each node handles in real-time.

```csharp
public class LoadBalancerService
{
    // Metrics gathering and evaluation
    private IMetricsGatherer _metricsGatherer;

    // Node registry for dynamic load balancing
    private INodeRegistry _nodeRegistry;

    public void DistributeLogEntries(IEnumerable<LogEntry> logEntries)
    {
        // Distribute the log entries based on the current node utilization metrics.
        var nodes = _nodeRegistry.GetNodes();
        foreach (var node in nodes)
        {
            // Distribute load based on node's availability and resource usage.
            _nodeRegistry.AssignLogEntriesToNode(node, logEntries);
        }
    }
}
```

2. Implement flexible queue sizes and backpressure mechanisms for each server node to manage incoming log entries optimizing throughput and memory usage under varying loads. Develop strategies to minimize latency spikes and ensure consistent service levels.

```csharp
