4. `mod logging`: Handles logging with configurable levels and formats.
5. `mod signal_handler`: Manages process signals effectively for graceful shutdown or reconnection.
6. Test files for each module to ensure proper functioning of the library.

**C Function (run_command.c):**

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <unistd.h>
#include <sys/wait.h>
#include <sys/types.h>
#include <signal.h>

pid_t run_command(const char *command) {
    pid_t pid;
    int status;
    pid = fork();

    if (pid == -1) {
        perror("fork failed");
        return 0;
    } else if (pid > 0) { // parent process
        waitpid(pid, &status, 0);
        return WIFEXITED(status) ? WEXITSTATUS(status) : 0;
    } else { // child process
        setsid();
        execl("/bin/sh", "sh", "-c", command, NULL);
        perror("execl failed");
        _exit(1);
    }
}
```

This library and C function outline should help you get started on your project. You can then implement the required features such as connection pooling, OAuth2 integration, exponential backoff, error handling, and monitoring based on this structure. Good luck with your coding task!']

