Please note that this is a starting point and requires additional components such as the RuleEngine, BattleStrategyApiClient, and event classes to be implemented according to your specific requirements.

This implementation uses Spring's caching annotation `@Cacheable`, Spring WebFlux for asynchronous processing with Mono, error handling using `onErrorResume`, timeouts, and the Spring Application Event Publisher for logging and monitoring purposes. The code is designed for extensibility and can be further optimized based on specific performance and scalability needs.']

[" Due to the extensive nature of this task, I will break it down into several manageable steps, each leading towards a complete Rust-based build tool.

1. File reading and writing in chunks:
```rust
use std::fs::File;
use std::io::{self, Read, Write};
use std::path::Path;

fn read_chunk<P: AsRef<Path>>(file: P, buf_size: usize) -> io::Result<Vec<u8>> {
    let mut file = File::open(file)?;
    let mut data = Vec::with_capacity(buf_size);
    let _ = file.read_to_end(&mut data).map(|_| {
        if data.len() < buf_size {
            let missing = buf_size - data.len();
            File::open(file)?.by_ref().take(missing).read_to_end(&mut data)?;
        }
        data
    });
    Ok(data)
}

fn write_chunk<P: AsRef<Path>>(file: P, buf: &[u8]) -> io::Result<()> {
    let mut file = File::create(file)?;
    let _ = file.write_all(buf);
    Ok(())
}
```

2. Incremental builds with caching strategies:
```rust
use std::collections::HashMap;

struct CompilationCache {
    cache: HashMap<String, String>,
}

impl CompilationCache {
    fn new() -> Self {
        Self {
            cache: HashMap::new(),
        }
    }

    fn get(&mut self, key: &str) -> Option<&'static str> {
        self.cache.get(key)
    }

    fn put(&mut self, key: String, value: String) {
        self.cache.insert(key, value);
    }
}
```

3. Parallelism and thread safety:
```rust
use std::sync::{Arc, Mutex};

struct SharedCompilationCache(Arc<Mutex<CompilationCache>>);

impl SharedCompilationCache {
    fn new() -> Self {
        Self(Arc::new(Mutex::new(CompilationCache::new())))
    }

    fn get(&self, key: &str) -> Option<&'static str> {
        let cache = self.0.lock().unwrap();
        cache.get(key)
    }

    fn put(&mut self, key: String, value: String) {
        let mut cache = self.0.lock().unwrap();
        cache.put(key, value);
    }
}
```

