5. Implement a soft delete mechanism with a configurable grace period using the `SoftDeleteManager` class:

```java
public class SoftDeleteManager {
    private final ResourceService resourceService;
    private final int gracePeriodSeconds;

    // constructor, setters and getters

    public void deleteResource(UUID id) {
        // mark resource for deletion with a timestamp
        resourceService.update(id, Resource.builder().deletedAt(Instant.now()).build());

        ScheduledExecutorService executor = Executors.newSingleThreadScheduledExecutor();
        AtomicBoolean deleted = new AtomicBoolean(false);

        executor.schedule(() -> {
            if (!deleted.get() && resourceService.retrieve(id).map(Resource::isDeleted).map(booleanValue -> !booleanValue).isEmpty()) {
                resourceService.delete(id);
                deleted.set(true);
            }
        }, gracePeriodSeconds, TimeUnit.SECONDS);
    }
}
```

6. Implement pagination by optimizing query execution plans and leveraging indexes where applicable in your data source implementations.

