2. JavaScript Function:

```javascript
function asyncReduce(arr, initialValue, callback) {
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    let reducedValue = initialValue;
    if (!Array.isArray(arr)) {
      throw new Error('Input must be an array');
    }
    const reducer = (accumulator, currentValue, currentIndex, arr) => {
      return callback(accumulator, currentValue, currentIndex, arr);
    };
    arr.reduce(reducer, reducedValue)
      .then(value => resolve(value))
      .catch(error => reject(error));
  });
}

// Sample Usage:
const numbers = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];
asyncReduce(numbers, 0, (accumulator, currentValue) => accumulator + currentValue).then(sum => console.log(`Sum of the array is: ${sum}`));
```

This function accepts an array, initial value, and callback function to perform asynchronous reduction operations on an array using JavaScript's `reduce()` method. The result will either be the final reduced value or an error if encountered during execution."]

